Z||000000||Steve Normington||04-11-2001||03:44 PM||||If anyone knows of a site or thread with the answer to this question, I'd appreciate a note.<P>What are the common items to fail on a 85 V-6 4-spd?  I'm not talking about the little stuff (headlight motors, A/C compressors), I'm talking about the stuff that requires a tow truck (shift fork arm, clutch slave cylinder bracket, etc).||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||04-11-2001||03:55 PM||||You'll probably be a victom of a pick-up coil going bad in your distributor.  That will stop you in your tracks as good as any. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  That and the coil itself take a lot of heat which tends to make them fail.  I've had one pick-up coil that was intermitant for a couple of days before it failed and one that failed while going through an intersection causing me to coast to the curb......NEXT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||04-11-2001||05:27 PM||||Ignition Module...<P>I would carry a spare and the tools to change it if you are taking a long trip in the car.  Seems to be a fairly common problem.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
