Z||000005||84Bill||04-11-2001||08:55 PM||||at any given time any and all the above could fail most common problems are with the sensors and modules that cause the engine to shake like a cold wet dog shittin razor blades but like any other older cars you can expect ANYTHING to crop up. <BR>Exibit A<BR> 84 Fiero<BR>PURCHACED: almost 2 weeks ago <BR>STATUS:    runs fine<BR>REPORT:<BR>Day 3 of ownership car dies on the way to work (figures) after a flawless weekend of grocery getting.<BR>CULPRIT<BR>Ignition module cost of 65 bucks incoured plus 50 bucks towing from brother inlaw (damn good thing)<BR>STATUS  Runs fine<BR>WEEK 1<BR>Oil change was performed old oil looks like it was in fair shape. pulled fuse to fuel pump and cranked engine to pump up oil DOH!!! wrong FUSE!!!! engine fires up and begins to run clatter of deflated lifter was noted engine was shut off and PROPER fuse removed, engine cranked until primed, engine fired up and rod knock was noted, wrench was thrown across garage bouncing off floor and through window on far side. cost 39 bucks for crank bearings and 17 or so for rod bearings and 3.75 for the glass cutter and this weekend shot to hell replacing said bearings. <P>CULPRIT: Idiot in neighbors yard looking for a wrench holding the supposed fuel pump fuse.<P>STATUS: vibrates so bad at 2500 to 4000 rpm that it rattled the mirror off the winshield and spun a wingnut off the aircleaner.<P>NOTES:<BR>I do love that 84 SE and I'll continue to fix those problems cuz I just like doing it. I thank god I am tallented enough to fix it myself.<BR> <BR>CLOSING STATEMENT<BR>So you see it can happen anytime any where and all at once would be most typical.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
