Z||000010||87GTZ34||04-13-2001||09:46 PM||||purchased an '87 GT identical to my first.<P>drove it 65 mi home and noted that @ 65mph bumps such as overpass joints caused some loss of control...<P>week 1 - start inspecting car for needed repairs:<P>  tune up stuff<BR>  exhaust manifold gaskets, no wait a minute, check that needed the manifold welded<BR>  brakes (everything all the way around)<P>  okay that should do it...<P>  repair back brakes as rivets are wearing groves in disk<P>  pull front manifold to repair it, DOH broke manifold bolt. okay pull head (and other head to change all upper gaskets.<P>  uh-oh a burned valve on number five. disassemble heads and inspect oh no wait, 3 other bad valves. now wait a minute that means 4 bad valves out of 6 hmmmm<P>heads need new springs and guides and one head didn't have rotators on the exhaust valve and the other did. hmmm  get everything fixed and reassemble.<P>while removing the alt the loose sheild grounds out the bat terminal and fries the fusible link. my bad, shouldv'e disconnected the bat first...<P>on assembly I notice the AC compressor only has 1 bolt out of 3 holding it on. remove compressor and retap front hole and reassemble (w/ 3 bolts).  <P>inspect the dogbone strut for alignment... wait a minute the cat melted the front tranny mount and the previous owner drove it for 65K mi and ripped apart the other 3 mounts. I guess that explains all the new emissions pieces on the car including the cat... Replace all 4 mounts. ouch (that is my head hitting crap under the car with bolts that are all overtightened...  While under the car I noted that the right inner CV cover was in two distinct pieces and grease was everywhere.  hmmm could that be from 4 bad mounts and the engine flopping around back there, and oh yeah would this cause the wheels to move orbitally when taking curves and hitting bumps....  replace passenger axle and inspect the drivers side. driver's side looks like it was replaced recently.  Noticed that the halfshaft spline was loose in the transaxle (that one will wait a week or two).<P>Okay reassemble the little stuff put the battery back in and fire it up. wait a minute what is pulling all of this current when I connect the batt (I couldv'e welded cast iron with that current).  The pos batt cable was rubbing the AC belt from the previous owner's mis-routing of the batt cables and the pos cable had a few bare spots. replace cable and re-connect.<P>week 4 - that's where I am now. Just started it tonight will drive it tomorrow if I didn't just jinx myself...<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 04-14-2001).]||||reg||1
